msgstr "Nearly. Hear the ones you missed below, then try again with Slower."

msgid "Nearly. Play the ones you missed once more."
msgstr "Nearly. Play the ones you missed once more."

msgid "On the hour"
msgstr "On the hour"

msgid "On the hour, say the hour alone: <et>kell on viis</et>, 5:00."
msgstr "On the hour, say the hour alone: <et>kell on viis</et>, 5:00."

msgid "On the hour: the number alone."
msgstr "On the hour: the number alone."

msgid "Other minutes, up to twenty past, count from the hour that has struck. <0/> is, word for word, “ten minutes, three passed”: 3:10. <1/> means through or past, and <2/> is the partitive of <3>minut</3>, the form after a number; lesson {partitive} explains it."
msgstr "Other minutes, up to twenty past, count from the hour that has struck. <0/> is, word for word, “ten minutes, three passed”: 3:10. <1/> means through or past, and <2/> is the partitive of <3>minut</3>, the form after a number; lesson {partitive} explains it."

